00:15:30.195 --> 00:15:32.398
to six months, maybe even a year,

00:15:32.398 --> 00:15:36.135
drill and ceremony
competitions are usually used

00:15:36.135 --> 00:15:38.837
to continue to motivate those individuals

00:15:38.837 --> 00:15:41.273
that have the longer periods of training.

00:15:41.273 --> 00:15:43.542
But not as likely in a
basic combat training

00:15:43.542 --> 00:15:46.845
because we're focusing on
shooting, moving, communicating,

00:15:46.845 --> 00:15:49.882
and treating yourself and
others on the battlefield.

00:15:49.882 --> 00:15:51.684
I'd have to say a four.

00:15:51.684 --> 00:15:56.422
Locate a wounded soldier,
represented by a dummy.

00:15:56.422 --> 00:15:59.858
You must then transport him to
the emergency field hospital.

00:15:59.858 --> 00:16:01.894
There's a lot going on there so far.

00:16:01.894 --> 00:16:04.763
When it started out, it
definitely was something

00:16:04.763 --> 00:16:06.966
that you would see in recruit training.

00:16:06.966 --> 00:16:09.902
You know, a lot of female leaders now

00:16:09.902 --> 00:16:13.939
are in positions of senior leadership,

00:16:13.939 --> 00:16:16.642
something that hadn't
occurred over many years,

00:16:16.642 --> 00:16:19.878
until the military had
started really opening up

00:16:19.878 --> 00:16:23.315
the ranks of the infantry
to our female leaders.

00:16:23.315 --> 00:16:25.918
An aggressor team will
be trying to stop you.

00:16:25.918 --> 00:16:28.287
They are all awaiting ranger training

00:16:28.287 --> 00:16:30.022
and can't wait to capture you.

00:16:31.090 --> 00:16:32.925
Based on what the information

00:16:32.925 --> 00:16:34.526
and the instructions they were given,

00:16:34.526 --> 00:16:38.397
it's actually an advanced
individual training.

00:16:38.397 --> 00:16:39.631
You know, medical training.

00:16:39.631 --> 00:16:42.501
They're not going to be
as complex with a mission

00:16:42.501 --> 00:16:44.269
that would go that deep,
and that was evident

00:16:44.269 --> 00:16:45.804
when I saw them in the river there,

00:16:45.804 --> 00:16:49.742
because the risk for, you
know, perhaps somebody drowning

00:16:49.742 --> 00:16:52.644
or something else with
all that equipment on,

00:16:52.644 --> 00:16:55.080
then not too many people
are going to want to

00:16:55.080 --> 00:16:58.017
put a recruit in that type of environment.

00:17:06.492 --> 00:17:09.661
Again, the risk factors
wouldn't be something

00:17:09.661 --> 00:17:11.497
that you'd see in recruit training,

00:17:11.497 --> 00:17:15.768
but definitely something
very similar challenging-wise

00:17:15.768 --> 00:17:18.504
as far as the military's concerned.

00:17:18.504 --> 00:17:20.239
You know, Marines have a Crucible,

00:17:20.239 --> 00:17:22.641
and the Army has this
thing called The Forge.

00:17:22.641 --> 00:17:27.279
Very similar, in the final
test of all of the training

00:17:27.279 --> 00:17:29.681
that they receive during
the recruit training.

00:17:29.681 --> 00:17:31.884
And there are medical lanes
where they might have to treat

00:17:31.884 --> 00:17:35.788
a casualty or transport a
casualty, like you saw here,

00:17:35.788 --> 00:17:37.756
to really see if all of the training

00:17:37.756 --> 00:17:42.194
has actually reached the
point where they are confident

00:17:42.194 --> 00:17:43.929
that these individuals can leave

00:17:43.929 --> 00:17:46.398
and go to their next assignment.

00:17:46.398 --> 00:17:49.101
I have to give that a
five as far as realism.

00:17:49.101 --> 00:17:52.037
♪ Casey Jones was a son of a b---- ♪

