This is depicting an
environment where there's still

00:18:03.916 --> 00:18:07.719
initial entry training or
initial military training,

00:18:07.719 --> 00:18:09.621
but it's Officer Candidate School.

00:18:09.621 --> 00:18:13.725
Typically, officer candidates
are a little bit more mature,

00:18:13.725 --> 00:18:16.662
have either been in the
military for quite some time

00:18:16.662 --> 00:18:18.330
and reached enlisted ranks.

00:18:18.330 --> 00:18:19.731
There's levels of hazing

00:18:19.731 --> 00:18:24.303
that may be more acceptable
in that environment

00:18:24.303 --> 00:18:26.004
versus in the recruit training.

00:18:26.004 --> 00:18:29.241
So there was a mandate
that provided leadership

00:18:29.241 --> 00:18:32.711
across all of the branches to come up with

00:18:32.711 --> 00:18:34.279
progressive ways, if you would,

00:18:34.279 --> 00:18:37.349
in order to attack and
get in front of hazing.

00:18:37.349 --> 00:18:41.153
And so whether it was
reporting, such as in the Army,

00:18:41.153 --> 00:18:44.056
you know, Not in My Squad,
to place accountability

00:18:44.056 --> 00:18:47.292
not just on leadership, but on each other.

00:18:47.292 --> 00:18:48.427
No, sir!

00:18:48.427 --> 00:18:49.261
Drill sergeant: DOR!

00:18:49.261 --> 00:18:50.329
I ain't gonna quit!

00:18:50.329 --> 00:18:52.064
Right, then you can forget it!

00:18:52.064 --> 00:18:53.031
You're out!

00:18:53.031 --> 00:18:54.766
Don't you do it!

00:18:54.766 --> 00:18:58.303
There's about two or three
layers of checks and balances

00:18:58.303 --> 00:19:01.840
so that you don't have that
